                at 2026-07-20T17:55:33.043564Z
                author "brendan@necessary.nu"
                kind @decision
                text "Operator decision (2026-07-20): the four parse-and-ignore CLI options are RESOLVED by deletion + one rewire, an intentional divergence from the reference CLI surface. Audit found: --dry-run (dead upstream too — gate removed in 2023), --out-matxin (no Matxin arm in either FormatConverter; silently emitted CG), and --show-tag-hashes (class-static stderr hash-dump; port hashes UTF-8 not UTF-16 so the numbers are meaningless, and it reintroduces the mutable-blob wart) all do NOTHING in the reference, so they are removed rather than transcribed. Only --debug did something upstream (~22 `debug_level > 1` read sites); it is rewired to raise the tracing level to DEBUG via a reloadable filter, and the unread cfg.debug_level/cfg.dry_run fields are deleted. Documented in options.rs (divergence note above the enum), cg_conv.rs, and README Scope."
            }
        )
