                        kind @note
                        text "Atomic by necessity, not by choice: parse_include -> parse_from_u_char -> parse_directive -> parse_include is a cycle through #include, and parse_contextual_test_list self-recurses (mod.rs:1460, 1579). 30 signatures change: 17 functions calling error_near/error_bare/inc_error_count directly (rules.rs 61 sites, mod.rs 36, driver.rs 17, parser_helpers 9 via trait), 10 transitive-only callers, 3 primitives. Terminates at parse_grammar_utf8 (driver.rs:740), already Result. Two traps: parse_from_u_char's directive loop CANNOT use `?` — recoverable errors are resumable, so it matches, records, restores the AST cursor, skipln and continues; and parse_grammar_data (driver.rs:610) still returns an error COUNT, plus increments error_counter directly at :719 without going through error_near — a fourth undocumented error channel to fold in."
