                        kind @note
                        text "Recorded as prose on [dec:cg3:grammar-source-sidecar] when the sidecar landed, but never given a node. Relabelling rewrites tags rather than rules, so the per-rule provenance stays accurate across the rewrite — the sidecar is not invalidated by relabelling, it is merely orphaned by the .cg3b identity stamp changing. So the fix is to re-stamp and re-emit the companion alongside the rewritten binary, not to regenerate provenance. Verified with the sidecar deliberately staled: the loader refuses it and degrades to the bare RT RULE line rather than quoting the wrong source, so today's behaviour is safe, just uninformative."
